+## Variations
+
+Interfaces, Experiences, Screens, Entities, Capabilities, Journeys and Business
+Rules share one relationship reading. Rows and tree rows show compact peer links and the shared subtype. Each resource Overview reads its own When used before behavior,
+with Experiment, Configuration or Version as a vocabulary-linked subtype.
+Variations uses the same compact cards as Also on. Opening a peer reads its full
+When used; navigation rows never repeat that prose.
+No dedicated collection, comparison or drawing is added. Peer links never alter
+ownership, tree expansion counts or the surrounding working view.
+
+The vocabulary has a dedicated Variations group for Variation, Experiment,
+Configuration, Version and When used. Definitions remain sourced from Model overview. When used is Markdown meaning, not an executable selector.
+Rule cards label conditional applicability, with full conditions in the Rule reading; lifecycle prohibition marks
+remain for unconditional prohibitions only. Conditional Rule restrictions remain
+reachable through the Rule lists and fact disclosures. No runtime permissions or
+selection decisions are inferred from applicability prose.
